    "question": {
      ":question/id": "753e5170-1c22-5a56-8505-16520685a533",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Write the following first-order linear ODE in standard form.\n\n$$\ny\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{x}^{2}y=2 x y^{2}\\,,\\ y\\ne 0\\,.\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "A first-order linear ODE is in standard form if it is written as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x)\\,,\n$$\n\nConverting the given equation to standard form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{x}^{2}y&=2 x y^{2} \\\\ y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{x}^{2}y-2 x y^{2}&=0 \\\\ y(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{x}^{2}-2 x y)&=0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{x}^{2}-2 x y&=0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\underbrace{(- 2 x)}_{P(x)}y&=\\underbrace{- x^{2}}_{Q(x)} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} - 2 x y&=- x^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the equation is written in standard form with $P(x)=- 2 x$ and $Q(x)=- x^{2}.$",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
