      ":question/problem": "Write the following first-order linear ODE in standard form.\n\n$$\n8 x\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2 x y-7 x=1+5 y\\,,\\ x\\ne 0\\,.\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "A first-order linear ODE is in standard form if it is written as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x).\n$$\n\nConverting the given equation to standard form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8 x\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2 x y-7 x&=1+5 y \\\\ 8 x\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+(2 x-5)y&=1+7 x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\underbrace{(\\frac{2 x - 5}{8 x})}_{P(x)}y&=\\underbrace{\\frac{7 x + 1}{8 x}}_{Q(x)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the equation is written in standard form with $P(x)=\\frac{2 x - 5}{8 x}$ and $Q(x)=\\frac{7 x + 1}{8 x}.$",
